---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' });

const faqJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Does a human decide the order creators appear in?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'No. Ranked lists on findbyface are ordered by FindRank, our engagement-based scoring system, not by an editor. Sponsored placements are the one exception, and those are always labeled.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can creators pay to change their FindRank score?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'No. Sponsorship buys a specific, disclosed placement (like a category page or search results), never a change to the underlying score. Sponsored cards are always marked "Sponsored" or "Ad".',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How often is the ranking updated?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Daily. We pull fresh engagement and pricing data every 24 hours and re-run FindRank, with verification status refreshed weekly.',
      },
    },
  ],
};
const jsonLd = JSON.stringify(faqJsonLd);
---

<Base
  title="How Our Search Engine Works | findbyface"
  description="How findbyface ranks OnlyFans creators with FindRank, how our AI face-match search works, and how sponsored placements are disclosed."
  canonical="https://findbyface.org/how-our-search-engine-works/"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={jsonLd} />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="prose-page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>How Our <span class="gradient-text">Search Engine</span> Works</h1>
      <p>An honest, plain-language look at how findbyface ranks and matches creators.</p>
      <p class="page-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Two different search systems</h2>
      <p>
        findbyface actually runs two separate systems, and it's worth being upfront about which
        one you're using. Browsing by category or typing a name into the search bar uses
        <strong>FindRank</strong>, our engagement-based ranking. Uploading a photo on the
        <a href="/onlyfans-finder-by-face/">face search tool</a> uses a completely different AI
        visual-matching pipeline. Neither one involves a person manually choosing results.
      </p>

      <h2>How FindRank works</h2>
      <p>
        FindRank orders creators by real engagement signals pulled live from OnlyFans — primarily
        favorited count and subscriber metrics. It's a straightforward popularity signal, not a
        subjective "quality" judgment: more real engagement moves a profile up, nothing else does.
        We re-pull this data and recalculate the ranking daily, so newly popular creators surface
        within a day rather than sitting behind a stale list. Verification badges are refreshed on
        a weekly cycle.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is <strong>no human review</strong> of ranking order. No one at findbyface manually
        bumps a profile up or down because of how it looks or who runs it. The only edits we ever
        make by hand are removals — for example, honoring a valid <a href="/dmca/">DMCA</a> request
        or a creator's own takedown request — never additions or reordering.
      </p>

      <h2>How face-match search works</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/onlyfans-finder-by-face/">photo search</a> is a separate AI pipeline, unrelated
        to FindRank. When you upload a photo, a face-recognition model detects the face and converts
        it into a numeric descriptor — a mathematical fingerprint of facial geometry. We compare that
        descriptor against creator profiles using vector similarity search and return the closest
        visual matches, ranked by similarity score. It runs on appearance alone: no names, no reverse
        lookups, and matches are for discovery, not identity confirmation. Read more in our
        <a href="/about/">About page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Sponsored placements, fully disclosed</h2>
      <p>
        findbyface is free to use, and part of how that's funded is paid placements: a creator can
        pay to appear in a specific spot, like the top of a category page or search results. We're
        direct about what that does and doesn't buy:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>It <strong>never</strong> changes a creator's FindRank score or face-match similarity score.</li>
        <li>It <strong>never</strong> hides, blurs, or demotes organic (unpaid) results to make room.</li>
        <li>Every sponsored card is labeled — you'll see a visible "Sponsored" or "Ad" tag, never a placement disguised as an organic result.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
      <p>
        We built findbyface to be a fast, honest way to browse and search OnlyFans creators, and we'd
        rather explain exactly how the list you're looking at was built than leave it a mystery. If
        something here doesn't match what you're seeing on the site, or you have questions we haven't
        covered, <a href="/contact/">reach out</a> — we'll answer directly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
